From f501f7815e9beaf044113d6c3501158ac6a7891e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaoyao Li <xiaoyao.li@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jul 2024 22:57:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 54/86] fixup: i386/tdx: Fix tdx_shared_bit()

For TDX, shared bit locates at the most significant bit of guest
physical address, i.e., the GPAW width.

GPAW is determined by  guest_phys_bits that
- when guest_phys_bits is 48, GPAW is 48 and shared bit locates at
  bit-47;
- when guest_phys_bits is 52, GPAW is 52 and shared bit locates at
  bit-51;

Signed-off-by: Xiaoyao Li <xiaoyao.li@intel.com>
---
 target/i386/kvm/tdx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/i386/kvm/tdx.c b/target/i386/kvm/tdx.c
index 9baeeaae67..38ba48ae5b 100644
--- a/target/i386/kvm/tdx.c
+++ b/target/i386/kvm/tdx.c
@@ -586,7 +586,7 @@ static void tdx_inject_interrupt(uint32_t apicid, uint32_t vector)
 
 static hwaddr tdx_shared_bit(X86CPU *cpu)
 {
-    return (cpu->phys_bits > 48) ? BIT_ULL(51) : BIT_ULL(47);
+    return (cpu->guest_phys_bits > 48) ? BIT_ULL(51) : BIT_ULL(47);
 }
 
 /* 64MB at most in one call. What value is appropriate? */
-- 
